# UI/UX Rules (Frontend only)

## Scope (IMPORTANT)

Applies ONLY to frontend UI implementation:

- Layout, spacing, typography, color, visuals
- Components and pages (React)
- Interaction patterns and UI states
- Accessibility (a11y)

Does NOT override:

- API contracts (`fullstack-contracts.mdc`)
- Security requirements (`security.mdc`)
- Testing requirements (`testing.mdc`)
- Universal code quality (`code-style.mdc`)
- Frontend architecture rules (`frontend-standards.mdc`)

## Use the installed skill

When building UI, strictly follow the UI/UX Pro Max skill installed in this repo under `.cursor/`.

## Required UI states (must)

For every async UI:

- loading (prefer skeleton)
- empty
- error (actionable message + retry)

For every form:

- field-level validation messages
- disabled states
- submit-in-progress state
- success/failure feedback

## Accessibility (must)

- Keyboard navigable
- Visible focus states
- aria-label for icon-only buttons
- Maintain readable contrast
- Avoid relying on color alone to convey meaning

## Layout & hierarchy (must)

- Mobile-first responsive layout
- Consistent spacing scale (avoid random pixel values)
- Clear information hierarchy (titles > sections > body)
- Use subtle elevation and separators for grouping (bento-like grouping is OK)

## Output format (preferred)

Before coding:

1. Component breakdown + state design
   Then:
2. Provide file-level changes with clear paths
